Z||000000||REDHOTT88||12-12-2001||02:59 PM||||I've heard a lot about the "Getrag" transmission. Is this a replacement tranny or do some Fieros come with them? (5 speeds?)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <P>How do you know if you have one, and why is it so popular?<P>How is it pronounced? GET rag, Jetrag, getrage? <P><BR>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over, runs smooth, shifts crisp!)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||12-12-2001||03:18 PM||||It came standard with the V6 starting in mid 86 with the introduction with the GT. Correct pronunciation = ??||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||12-12-2001||03:48 PM||||Pronounced Muncie  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>The muncie had a dipstick/fill in the trans the Isuzu you had to remove the vss to fill.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroman_5000||12-12-2001||04:23 PM||||I pronounce it   gEt-rag  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000004||Steve Normington||12-12-2001||04:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>It came standard with the V6 starting in mid 86 with the introduction with the GT. Correct pronunciation = ??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>[nitpick]The GT was introduced in 1985. The fastback was introduced in mid 86. [/nitpick] I pronounce it Geh-trag.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||12-12-2001||05:02 PM||||Most people pronounce it GET-RAG, but officially it is GUH-TRAHG (long "A" sound, like AAAH).<P>I remember seeing a dealer promotional video from the factory and this is how they pronounced it.  Personally I like GET-RAG better.......the "proper" way sounds too formal/Alex Trebek-ish.<P><BR>Mike ||||reg||1
Z||000006||REDHOTT88||12-12-2001||05:11 PM||||I like get-rag too. I just didn't want to sound dumb, in case I met Alex Trebek!! Ha Ha   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>So I probably have a Getrag in my 88 Formula, Huh?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P> Why is this called a muncie as well? (Like I originally said, Dumb questions....)<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
