Z||000012||StuGood||12-13-2001||12:22 PM||||One of the easier ways to tell a Getrag transaxle: it has a steel end plate on the outboard (driver's side) end.  The Isuzu 5-speed and Muncie 4-speed are aluminum there; Mr. Magnet will tell you what you've got.<P>I wondered about the pronunciation of Getrag, too. I suspeced that the first "G" in Getrag was a hard G, like the first "g" in "garage."  And the 2nd "g" in Getrag was a soft g - like the 2nd "g" in "garage!"  So I contacted an associate in Everett, WA, whose boss (an old proud-to-be-of-German-descent guy) confirmed my suspicions.  The proud German-American boss seemed to be familiar with Getrag, too.   ||||reg||6
